From 17f25cf735e523f7f531e90204bcb3e15c0d9334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:33:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 096/113] rust: drm: expose HDCP 2.2 message identifiers

Add a DRM display module with typed identifiers for the standard HDCP 2.2 protocol messages. Transport drivers can use the canonical drm_hdcp.h values without reaching into generated bindings.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
 rust/kernel/drm/display.rs      |  5 +++
 rust/kernel/drm/display/hdcp.rs | 54 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 rust/kernel/drm/mod.rs          |  1 +
 3 files changed, 60 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 rust/kernel/drm/display.rs
 create mode 100644 rust/kernel/drm/display/hdcp.rs

diff --git a/rust/kernel/drm/display.rs b/rust/kernel/drm/display.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..007ed284c551
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rust/kernel/drm/display.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
